  "body": "Historical audit replay depended on CPython float summation and local timezone availability, causing six Ubuntu CI failures despite local Windows passes. This repair makes the historical execution contract explicit while preserving every archived artifact and existing expected hash. **HOLD: no independent reviewer is designated; no PR may be merged or approved on the owner's behalf.**\n\nThe common repair is also integrated into actual PR #44, #45 and #46 heads so their own cumulative trees pass CI. This PR retains the repair commits, merges those repaired dependencies and adds field-level diagnostics and verification evidence. Against repaired #46, the remaining delivery diff is evidence, documentation and one byte-preserving attribute rule. It targets main as required; inherited dependency files are not new repair scope.\n\n## Root causes and behavior\n\n- Three Week 7 tests: eight metric float leaves differ between Python 3.11 sequential and 3.12 compensated summation.\n- Week 8 audit: two week metrics and 346 cross-week metrics change two generated manifest hashes; no actual contradictory status or missing checksum was found.\n- Week 8 research: fourteen float leaves differ for the same arithmetic reason.\n- Week 9 context: 216 timezone offset/status leaves differ when system/package tzdata is present. Fresh Windows CI also reproduces this; it is not exclusively a Linux issue.\n\nThe largest native metric difference is 2.842170943040401e-14. The repaired verifier accepts **zero** byte differences. There is no numerical tolerance, output replacement, expected-hash edit, grade/rank/confidence change, policy promotion or schema change. New adversarial tests reject altered inputs, locked lines, statuses, checksum coverage, metric mutations and context provenance. Existing assertions remain; five test files route replay through the isolated compatibility modules.\n\n## Verification\n\n| PR | Successful run | Tests in each of four environments |\n|---|---|---:|\n| #44 | [41102004369](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41102004369) | 791 |\n| #45 | [41102071702](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41102071702) | 841 |\n| #46 | [41102087073](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41102087073) | 850 |\n\nLocal Windows Python 3.12.14: **850 passed, 39 existing warnings, 457.95s**, tested commit `d2a2883f6acb33aea829e85ad4117baac1e85e87`. Five suite/safety/migration/replay commands and four additional seal/scoring/PDF/owner-review gates passed. All 23 exact output hashes match the CI platforms, including all six context versions. All 125 applicable protected files match; #44 has 70, with 55 later files absent from its original scope. Historical whitespace remains explicitly recorded (6,421 findings); new delivery diff passes `git diff --check`.\n\nFinal delivery source: `0d9a4b56bd49e3fbef4326aa7a5bd6eec9d13e29`; tested merge candidate `77f790c07e875a4c0dd37841cd148ea6c74544fc`. [Final CI 41483657531](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/actions/runs/41483657531) **PASSED all four jobs: 850 tests per environment, zero failures, and all safety/migration/exact replay gates passed.** All 23 archived output hashes agree across the four CI environments and local Windows 3.12.14. Final-head CI is now complete; independent review remains the merge blocker. The earlier implementation pass at `9f310e1` and local `d2a2883` result are separate runs.\n\n[Full report, exact files, commands, source/merge SHAs, limitations and rollback](https://github.com/JCRABURN/cfb-betting-system-v3/blob/0d9a4b56bd49e3fbef4326aa7a5bd6eec9d13e29/docs/CROSS_PLATFORM_REPLAY_REPAIR.md). Machine-readable per-field comparisons, original baseline logs, complete successful CI artifacts and local receipts are in `outputs/2026-cross-platform-replay/`, with a 501-file evidence manifest. No unrelated implementation changes; root NFL work and original repository untouched.\n\n## Remaining gates and rollback\n\nIndependent approval must cover the tested cumulative repaired dependencies and this repair. Logical ancestors #41/#42/#43 are not separately certified by these runs; prefer reviewed cumulative #44 -> #45 -> #46 -> #47, refreshing CI after any base change. No author review substitution. Preserve v2.8, pending contest approval and INCOMPLETE historical CLV. The six non-CI workflows stay disabled; no security settings or secrets changed. The expired Week 9 pregame automation is paused with no postgame collection.\n\nRollback is a reviewed revert of only the new verification modules, test routing and CI extension, retaining all evidence/history. No database migration or historical artifact needs reversal. Do not reactivate production workflows.\n\n\nCI dependency note: Python requirements are unchanged. The new actions/upload-artifact@v4 workflow action stores the read-only replay comparisons needed for review; it uses the MIT license (https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/blob/v4/LICENSE). Its operational scope is CI artifact publication, with no application runtime or production effect. The v4 tag is mutable, as are the existing action tags; exact runner/action versions remain in job logs, and archived SHA256 comparisons fail closed if behavior changes.\n",
